<Folder><name>Day 2 — KEF → Snaefellsnes</name>
<Placemark><name>KEF Airport</name><description>Day 2: Arrive 6:35 AM. Pick up car</description><styleUrl>#day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-22.606,63.985,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Borgarnes</name><description>Day 2: Coffee + bakery</description><styleUrl>#day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-21.921,64.537,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Gerðuberg Cliffs</name><description>Day 2: Basalt columns</description><styleUrl>#day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-22.348,64.754,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ytri-Tunga Beach</name><description>Day 2: Seal colony!</description><styleUrl>#day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-23.24,64.77,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hotel Búðir</name><description>Day 2: Check in. Black Church</description><styleUrl>#day2</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-23.38,64.82,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 3 — SOLAR ECLIPSE</name>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 4 — Búðir → Deildartunguhver → Golden Circle → Ranga</name>
<Placemark><name>Deildartunguhver</name><description>Day 4: Europe's most powerful hot spring (~25 min, viewing only)</description><styleUrl>#day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-21.411,64.663,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hraunfossar &amp; Barnafoss (optional)</name><description>Day 4: Lava-field waterfalls — optional +1h detour</description><styleUrl>#day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-20.978,64.702,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mika Restaurant</name><description>Day 4: Lunch 15:00 · Conf #8934174</description><styleUrl>#day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-20.3,64.31,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Strokkur Geysir</name><description>Day 4: Erupts every 6-10 min</description><styleUrl>#day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-20.302,64.313,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Gullfoss</name><description>Day 4: "Golden Falls"</description><styleUrl>#day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-20.123,64.327,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hotel Ranga</name><description>Day 4: Relaxed evening · observatory</description><styleUrl>#day4</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-20.52,63.83,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 5 — Thorsmork + Katla</name>
<Placemark><name>Þórsmörk Valley</name><description>Day 5: 6h superjeep — Waterproof hiking boots — trail walking, damp ground; guide fords the rivers</description><styleUrl>#day5</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-19.51,63.68,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Katla Ice Cave</name><description>Day 5: 3h guided — Ice cave — tour supplies crampons + helmet; wear warm waterproof boots</description><styleUrl>#day5</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-19.1,63.625,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 6 — Waterfalls → Reynisfjara → Klaustur</name>
<Placemark><name>Seljalandsfoss + Gljúfrabúi</name><description>Day 6: Walk behind + hidden Gljufrabui — You walk BEHIND the falls + wet path to Gljúfrabúi — waterproof jacket and grippy shoes</description><styleUrl>#day6</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-19.993,63.616,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Skógafoss</name><description>Day 6: 370 steps to top — 370 steep steps to the top — sturdy shoes</description><styleUrl>#day6</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-19.511,63.532,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Dyrhólaey</name><description>Day 6: Sea arch, puffins, viewpoint — Uneven clifftop — sturdy shoes</description><styleUrl>#day6</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-19.128,63.401,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Reynisfjara</name><description>Day 6: Black sand, basalt columns — Deadly sneaker waves — never turn your back to the sea; stay well back</description><styleUrl>#day6</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-19.065,63.405,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Vík</name><description>Day 6: Lunch in Vik</description><styleUrl>#day6</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-19.006,63.419,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Fjaðrárgljúfur Canyon</name><description>Day 6: Moss-covered gorge (45 min) — Rim trail, can be muddy — sturdy shoes</description><styleUrl>#day6</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-18.172,63.771,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Magma Hotel (Kirkjubæjarklaustur)</name><description>Day 6: Aug 15-16 · Conf EW78CP66MN</description><styleUrl>#day6</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-18.085,63.772,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 7 — Glacier Hike → Fosshotel (relax)</name>
<Placemark><name>Skaftafell — Glacier Hike</name><description>Day 7: Crampons on Vatnajokull (3.5h) — Stiff hiking boots REQUIRED — crampons strap on. Warm + waterproof. Rentals if needed</description><styleUrl>#day7</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-16.966,64.016,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Svínafellsjökull</name><description>Day 7: Crevassed glacier tongue viewpoint — Uneven glacier-tongue viewpoint — sturdy shoes</description><styleUrl>#day7</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-16.88,64.0,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Fosshotel Glacier Lagoon</name><description>Day 7: Hot tub + rest. Glacier views</description><styleUrl>#day7</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-16.752,63.955,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 8 — Jokulsarlon Zodiac → Retreat</name>
<Placemark><name>Jökulsárlón — Zodiac 9:20 AM</name><description>Day 8: Morning boat among the icebergs — Boat gives you a warm flotation suit — dress warm underneath; expect splashes</description><styleUrl>#day8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-16.231,64.078,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Diamond Beach</name><description>Day 8: Ice on black sand — morning walk (or golden hour Day 7 eve)</description><styleUrl>#day8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-16.178,64.044,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Stokksnes / Vestrahorn (optional)</name><description>Day 8: Iconic photo spot — adds ~3h</description><styleUrl>#day8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-14.967,64.247,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Höfn (optional)</name><description>Day 8: Langoustine lunch</description><styleUrl>#day8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-15.207,64.254,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Blue Lagoon Retreat</name><description>Day 8: Spa. Lava dinner!</description><styleUrl>#day8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-22.449,63.88,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 9 — Spa → Thingvellir → Reykjavik</name>
<Placemark><name>The Retreat — Spa</name><description>Day 9: Long spa + breakfast until 11:00</description><styleUrl>#day9</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-22.445,63.882,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Þingvellir</name><description>Day 9: Walk between tectonic plates</description><styleUrl>#day9</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-21.129,64.256,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Reykjavík</name><description>Day 9: Hallgrimskirkja, Harpa, Laugavegur</description><styleUrl>#day9</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-21.943,64.147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 10 — Reykjanes Peninsula → Fly</name>
<Placemark><name>Bridge Between Continents</name><description>Day 10: Two tectonic plates</description><styleUrl>#day10</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-22.677,63.868,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
